Z||000000||Ironhorse||07-15-2000||01:02 PM||||I found out that the reason that F-15 won't run is becuase of Ignition moudles. I purchased one and to be safe, I also bought dist pick up unit. And it run. now here's another problem.  When you first start it, it  idle at 1000rpm then in 3 sec, it shot up to 3500 rpm and stay there. With that I immeadiately turn the key off.  I've done this several time to see if it would change in the course. Nope.  I'm scare and have no clue as of what going on.  The engine light diagnostic said that it's the map sensor, but in my past experience if the map goes bad, it just idle real low and die when you give it gas.  This is what happened on the old engine, it idle at 3000 rpm and in 2 min felt a loud thud, it threw a rod.   I DO NOT WANT THE SAME THING HAPPEN ON THIS NEW engine that I have. I've already spent 1500 dollar and spent 3 month building it.  Any help any suggestion. TIA||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||07-15-2000||02:06 PM||||Disconnect battery to reset codes. Then put ECM in bypass mode (short the 2 pins on ALDL connector)Start engine and check timing. If that is good you may need to drive it over 40mph to reset the IAC sensor. Also When checking the timing while ECM is in bypass mode see if the idle shoots up. If it doesn't it's definately a sensor problem.||||reg||1
