Z||000009||Oreif||07-17-2000||01:51 AM||||You could try pulling the IAC out first and cleaning the port and the spindle of the IAC. Be careful not to turn the spindle of the IAC this is an adjustment. This may correct your 5 - 6 second die time.<BR>Upon replacing or cleaning the IAC your idle will bump up to 1500 - 2000 until the ECM resets it, which happens when the vehicle is in drive and travelling about 40 - 45 mph.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 07-17-2000).]||||reg||1
