Z||000011||lowCG||07-17-2000||04:20 PM||||If there's a way to drive the car,it might re-set something and make the MAP error go-away,worth a try if you know that the cooling system is all topped off and ready to go,and that the oil pressure is there.<BR>That way you could keep the revs down by keeping a slight load on the engine,which is how you want to initially break in your engine anyways.<BR>Pontiacs have funky oiling systems;the crank/rods are the last thing to get oil!<BR>That may be why the last one died.<BR>I'm having the same problem with a new install,and my speedo wires are screwed up,so I need to fix that before the computer can then fix itself hopefully.<BR>||||reg||1
